# CL + Spec Kit Integration

**Hook:** `integration.cl_spec`, `spec.flow`, `memory.agents_md`, `integration.wiring_audit`

- `AGENTS.md` stores **operational** facts (commands, paths, conventions), not product behavior.
- Behavioral changes (APIs, acceptance criteria, requirements) belong in the active `spec.md` first.
- Do not promote Continual Learning bullets that describe **what the system must do** into durable memory.
- Before memory promotion, complete the **Integration wiring audit** (`.cursor/rules/integration-wiring-audit.mdc`).
- If a propose/ingest step rejects a candidate as behavioral, update the active spec before retrying.

See project `docs/cl-spec-integration.md` or equivalent integration doc when present.
